Maura kept track of the number of games her soccer team won each year. According to the table, what was the rate of change between 2017 and 2018? (Unit: games per year)
Assistant: Plug the numbers into the formula for rate of change and simplify.
Rate of change
 = \frac{change in value}{change in time}
 = \frac{8 games - 50 games}{2018 - 2017}
 = \frac{8 games - 50 games}{1 year}
 = \frac{-42 games}{1 year}
 = -42 games per year
